% holding-blocked: The original is fully notated with words on every note, and the listening link is Gamelan Sekar Jaya's own channel, but it has not been tried with students. A Grade 2 classroom teacher must trial the switch from quick bell sounds to long gong sounds, the bordun and the held notes at 76-88; an Indonesian (Balinese) gamelan educator must review the framing, the choice of "Legong Lasem" (a dance whose roots are sacred) and the history in the video's own description; a second score reader must check the notes, words and cues.
